ID: Ch6-Better
TEXT:

"Maybe it would indeed be better to keep your distance for now."

"Perhaps," Rose murmurs. "Time might cool the blood between our kinds. But thank you for listening, Barry. Carrying it alone wasn't doing me any favors."

A softer, genuine smile touches her face.

"Glad to help," I say.

We haven't cleared a quarter mile before Daren falls in beside me, eyeing the weapon lashed to my frame.

"Barry. Why is that crossbow riding the outside of your rucksack?"

"Because the canvas is packed solid to the drawstring."

