ID: Ch6-Travel
TEXT:

#if(v_ch2_human_reason == 1) {
Kate walks with a different posture than she did yesterday. When she first joined us, every muscle was coiled like a spring, her eyes constantly checking the brush as if waiting for us to draw steel the second her back was turned. Today she lets the tension slip. A faint, real smile touches her mouth when she talks to Rose, answering questions about mosses and cold-weather roots with something resembling ease.

We keep a steady south-bound rhythm, pausing only to knock wild pears from the higher branches or dip our flasks into passing streams. During one of those water stops, Rose catches my eye and drops back beside me under the shade of a weeping cedar.

"Barry," she murmurs, keeping her voice low. "I have to ask. Did Daren and I walk in on something important between you and Kate this morning? She turns cold every time I bring it up. I'd hate to think we ruined an honest confession because neither of us knew how to read a room."

}
#if(v_ch5_admit_lie == 0 && v_ch2_human_reason != 1) {
Kate walks with a different posture than she did yesterday. When she first joined us, every muscle was coiled like a spring, her eyes constantly checking the brush as if waiting for us to draw steel the second her back was turned. Today she lets the tension slip. A faint, real smile touches her mouth when she talks to Rose, answering questions about mosses and cold-weather roots with something resembling ease.

Daren, meanwhile, has treated me like dead weight on the trail. Not a single word since we left the clearing. The Magium confession sits between us like a wall of cold stone.

Rose has tried three separate times to coax him into conversation, but all she gets in return are clipped, monosyllabic grunts.

We keep a steady south-bound rhythm, pausing only to knock wild pears from the higher branches or dip our flasks into passing streams. During one of those water stops, Rose catches my eye and drops back beside me under the shade of a weeping cedar.

"Barry," she murmurs, keeping her voice low. "I have to ask. Did Daren and I walk in on something important between you and Kate this morning? She turns cold every time I bring it up. I'd hate to think we ruined an honest confession because neither of us knew how to read a room."

}
#if(v_ch5_admit_lie == 1 && v_ch5_ignore_scream == 1 && v_ch2_human_reason != 1) {
