ID: Ch6-Flirt
TEXT:

#if(v_ch6_flirt == 1) {
"Don't worry, that wasn't what our discussion was about."

Rose arches an auburn brow, clearly unconvinced. "If you say so! Though if both of you insist nothing happened, I won't pry. Come on—we should help gather fruit. We have miles of empty road ahead."

}
#if(v_ch6_flirt == 2) {
"Honestly? I've been staring at you all morning instead of watching the trail. I tripped twice."

Rose blinks, then lets out a delighted laugh that turns heads fifty paces away.

"My, aren't we forward!" she says, her eyes dancing with amusement. "Tell me, Barry—has that approach ever worked for you in the past?"

}
#if(v_ch6_flirt == 3) {
"I'm still available, if that's what you're asking."

A slow, knowing smile touches Rose's lips.

"That wasn't what I was asking, but it does answer my question. You wouldn't be making a pass at me if your heart were tied to Kate. As for your advances—I'm not married, so I have no reason to outright turn you down before I get to know you, but I'd rather we postpone this conversation until a later date. Does that sound okay to you?"

}
#if(v_ch6_flirt == 4) {
"Kate and I have a purely professional relationship. She threatens to kill me, I fail to die."

Rose presses a hand against her collarbone, laughing softly.

"Oh my, that's quite the arrangement! Though from what I've seen, there might be a bit more warmth behind those threats than you're letting on. Perhaps we should take this a bit slower? Get to know each other first?"

}
#if(v_ch6_flirt == 5) {
"Don't worry, we got to say all we needed before you interrupted."

Rose's smile softens into something warm and understanding. "Ah. That explains why Kate was avoiding the subject, then. I'm glad that the two of you are being honest with each other. I won't ask any more questions. However, I will tell you this: I've only known Kate for a few hours, but I can tell that she's been through a lot. So please, try not to hurt her. She has a good heart."

"I'll... keep that in mind."

Rose smiles.

"Now then, I think we should start helping the others with picking fruits. We'll need all the food we can get for the long journey ahead of us."

}
#if(v_ch6_flirt == 6) {
"Actually, you're the one that stunned me with your beauty when I first saw you."

Rose catches her breath, a flush rising across her cheeks. "Oh... Thank you for the compliment, but I thought—"

"There's nothing going on between me and Kate," I say plainly. "In fact, the purpose of our discussion this morning was to clear things up between us, because of Daren's joke that I was smitten with her."

"I see. I guess I misunderstood the situation, then. Listen, about what you said earlier, I don't—"

"There's no need to say anything," I tell her. "I wasn't making a pass at you, I was just being sincere. I barely even know you besides the fact that you seem really nice and kind. I think we should continue this conversation after we've known each other a little better."

Rose's smile returns, bright and genuine.

"Yeah, we should do that!"

She steps back toward the orchard trees.

"I think we should go help the others with picking fruits. We'll need all the food we can get for the long journey ahead of us."

}
choice("Continue", Ch6-Backstory, v_current_scene = Ch6-Backstory) if (v_ch6_flirt == 1 || v_ch6_flirt == 5 || v_ch6_flirt == 6)
choice(""Every single time."", Ch6-Single, v_current_scene = Ch6-Single) if (v_ch6_flirt == 2)
choice(""Not really."", Ch6-Really, v_current_scene = Ch6-Really) if (v_ch6_flirt == 2)
choice(""Of course."", Ch6-Course, v_current_scene = Ch6-Course) if (v_ch6_flirt == 3)
