choice("Continue", Ch6-Villain, v_current_scene = Ch6-Villain)


ID: Ch6-Villain
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 0) {
Kate fires a volley of several hundred sharp ice blades toward the dragon, but the points shatter harmlessly against its armored scales.

"Kate!" Daren shouts from above. "Can you—NGHHH—make a slide for me?"

"Hold on!" Kate sweeps both arms across the clearing, quickly building a steep ice slide that angles from below his feet down to the grass beside us.

Daren drives his broadsword furiously into the dragon's claw. The beast roars in pain, dropping him squarely onto the slide, and he hits the turf next to us.

The dragon wheels instantly, unleashing a torrent of fire aimed directly at Kate. She floats a thick shield of ice above her head to catch the blast. Steam roars off the surface as the heat bores through the frost, Kate straining with every ounce of will to hold the barrier.

Daren scrambles to her side, raising his shield to cover her before the ice gives out. But the morning's wounds have drained his reserves; the white barrier shatters with an ear-splitting crack, and his shield falls into the dirt. The blast of compressed air flings Rose across the clearing, her skull striking a boulder. She lies motionless in the smoking grass.

Think, Barry. Think. What can you do to turn the tide? There has to be something. A leverage point, an angle, anything. Think!

"It's over, humans," the dragon shouts triumphantly from high above. "Your era is at an end. I am going to exterminate every single one of you, until all that remains of your race is a forgotten memory. And I'm saving Eiden for last."

The stat device in my pocket is worthless here. Even with every attribute maxed, I wouldn't last five seconds.

The dragon opens its jaws, and a wall of fire pours down on us. I close my eyes, awaiting the end.

Seconds pass.

No heat.

I open my eyes.

The dragon's flames hang frozen in mid-air, a handspan from my face, suspended like glowing glass. Beyond them, everything has stopped. Daren, Kate, and Rose stand motionless. The wind is gone.

"Seriously, now," a familiar voice drawls behind me. "How could I have let him win after saying a line like that?"

I turn around. Eiden stands three paces away, eyes closed, hands in his pockets, smiling.

"I mean, I don't think I've even read a children's book where the main villain gloats to such an extent. It's embarrassing, really."

}
#if(v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 1) {
Kate fires a volley of several hundred sharp ice blades toward the dragon, but the points shatter harmlessly against its armored scales.

"Kate!" Daren shouts from above. "Can you—NGHHH—make a slide for me?"

"Hold on!" Kate sweeps both arms across the clearing, quickly building a steep ice slide that angles from below his feet down to the grass beside us.

Daren drives his broadsword furiously into the dragon's claw. The beast roars in pain, dropping him squarely onto the slide, and he hits the turf next to us.

Casting so many spells in rapid succession drains Kate's last reserves. Weakened by the morning's crossbow wound, she gasps for breath, her right hand trembling violently.

The dragon wheels instantly, unleashing a torrent of fire aimed directly at Kate. She floats a thick shield of ice above her head to catch the blast.

The heat bores through the frost in a heartbeat. The shield melts into boiling steam, and the flames engulf her left arm and half of her face. A raw scream tears from her throat, but she bites it down and flash-freezes the fire to extinguish it. The burn leaves a raw, blistered wound across the entire left side of her face, but her eyes never leave the sky. Her resolve hardens into iron.

She readies another ice shield for the next strike.

Daren scrambles to her side, raising his shield to cover her before the ice gives out. But the morning's wounds have drained his reserves; the white barrier shatters with an ear-splitting crack, and his shield falls into the dirt. The blast of compressed air flings Rose across the clearing, her skull striking a boulder. She lies motionless in the smoking grass.

Think, Barry. Think. What can you do to turn the tide? There has to be something. A leverage point, an angle, anything. Think!

"It's over, humans," the dragon shouts triumphantly from high above. "Your era is at an end. I am going to exterminate every single one of you, until all that remains of your race is a forgotten memory. And I'm saving Eiden for last."

The stat device in my pocket is worthless here. Even with every attribute maxed, I wouldn't last five seconds.

The dragon opens its jaws, and a wall of fire pours down on us. I close my eyes, awaiting the end.

Seconds pass.

No heat.

I open my eyes.

The dragon's flames hang frozen in mid-air, a handspan from my face, suspended like glowing glass. Beyond them, everything has stopped. Daren, Kate, and Rose stand motionless. The wind is gone.

"Seriously, now," a familiar voice drawls behind me. "How could I have let him win after saying a line like that?"

I turn around. Eiden stands three paces away, eyes closed, hands in his pockets, smiling.

"I mean, I don't think I've even read a children's book where the main villain gloats to such an extent. It's embarrassing, really."

}
choice(""Where have you been hiding all this time?"", Ch6-Time-weaver, v_current_scene = Ch6-Time-weaver, v_ch6_eiden_answer = 1)
choice(""What did you do?"", Ch6-Time-weaver, v_current_scene = Ch6-Time-weaver, v_ch6_eiden_answer = 2)
choice(""Why did you save us?"", Ch6-Time-weaver, v_current_scene = Ch6-Time-weaver, v_ch6_eiden_answer = 3)


ID: Ch6-Time-weaver
TEXT:

#if(v_ch6_eiden_answer == 1) {
"Where have you been hiding all this time?"

"Now, now, Barry, is this any way to talk to your savior?" Eiden tilts his head, smiling. "To answer your question, I've been following this dragon for a while now. I've been masking my presence so that he couldn't find  me by using his sight, smell, hearing or magical sense. I've been watching your battle since it began and I must say, I am not very impressed."

"Are you kidding me? What do you expect me to do against a dragon?"

"How about using that device you're holding in your hand?"

"Yeah? And what would you have me do? Max my strength and punch him to death?"

"Um... excuse me... sir..."

Me and Eiden both turn around at the same time and see that Rose is standing up and looking at Eiden, confused.

"Um... Hi... My name is Rose. Are you a friend of Barry?"

Eiden furrows his brows, and makes a hand gesture towards Rose.

"W-What are you doing?" Rose asks him.

"Interesting," Eiden says. "Rose, I've cast a spell that is supposed to freeze time for everyone except me and Barry. Have you by any chance studied time magic in your lifetime?"

"Uh.. no, I can't cast any magic at all. I'm not a mage."

Eiden's smile widens.

"Then I offer you my sincerest congratulations. As of this moment, you are officially a time weaver!"

"A... what?"

Eiden turns to me.

"Barry, I must admit, I don't think I've ever seen such diversity in a team before. A time weaver, a healer in armor, a survivor from the Beacon of Hope and a stat device wielder. I think I'm starting to root for you!"

}
#if(v_ch6_eiden_answer == 2) {
"What did you do?"

"I'd say this should all be self explanatory. I've frozen time."

"Frozen ti-- How is that even possible?"

"There is no such thing as impossible, Barry. As long as you never stop believing in yourself, you can overcome any limits. Remember this advice!"

"Is this all a joke to you?"

"No, but your fight with the dragon was. I've been watching your battle since it began and I must say, I am not very impressed."

"Are you kidding me? What do you expect me to do against a dragon?"

"How about using that device you're holding in your hand?"

"Yeah? And what would you have me do? Max my strength and punch him to death?"

