The dragon splits into three shimmering copies, each one circling in a different direction. I strain to track the real one—shadows, light angles, the faint displacement of air. The illusion is too tight, too layered. Only raw perception, premonitive instinct, or reflexes fast enough to react blind could separate the decoy from the kill stroke.

#if(v_ch6_offense == 1 && v_perception == 4 || v_ch6_improvise == 1 && v_perception == 4 && v_ch6_offense != 2) {

The sunlight glinting off the dragon's crimson scales strikes from the wrong angle—the shadows fall toward the sun. A glamour.

I cast true sight. The illusion evaporates, revealing the real Tyrath closing in from my right flank.

I clap my hands together, releasing a concussive blast of air that slams into his snout and drives him back fifty feet.

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 2 && v_perception == 4) {

The sunlight glinting off the dragon's crimson scales strikes from the wrong angle—the shadows fall toward the sun. A glamour.

I cast true sight. The illusion evaporates, revealing the real Tyrath closing in from my right flank.

I teleport directly beside him and swing Daren's blade. Taken by surprise, the dragon teleports away before the steel can land.

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 1 && v_premonition == 4 && v_perception < 4 || v_ch6_improvise == 1 && v_premonition == 4 && v_perception < 4 && v_ch6_offense != 2) {

A phantom image flashes behind my eyes: the dragon in front of me dissolving while a second shadow drops from above. Premonition.

I cast true sight. The decoy in front of me vanishes, revealing the real Tyrath closing in from my right flank.

I clap my hands together, releasing a concussive blast of air that slams into his snout and drives him back fifty feet.

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 2 && v_premonition == 4 && v_perception < 4) {

A phantom image flashes behind my eyes: the dragon in front of me dissolving while a second shadow drops from above. Premonition.

I cast true sight. The decoy in front of me vanishes, revealing the real Tyrath closing in from my right flank.

I teleport directly beside him and swing Daren's blade. Taken by surprise, the dragon teleports away before the steel can land.

}
#if(v_perception < 4 && v_premonition < 4 && v_reflexes < 4) {

I loose a lightning bolt straight into his chest. The arc grounds across his scales with zero effect. The silhouette in front of me vanishes like smoke.

A spiked tail whips out of blind space behind me, coiling around my torso. The constricting grip crushes my ribs, driving the air from my lungs.

"You are not the only one who casts magic, human," the dragon rumbles in my ear.

The pressure spikes. Organs rupture. Blood fills my mouth, warmth running down my chin as my vision darkens to a pinprick. The last thing I register is the dragon's slit eyes and mocking laughter.

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 1 && v_reflexes == 4 && v_perception < 4 && v_premonition < 4 || v_ch6_improvise == 1 && v_reflexes == 4 && v_perception < 4 && v_premonition < 4 && v_ch6_offense != 2) {

I loose a lightning bolt straight into his chest. The arc grounds across his scales with zero effect. The silhouette vanishes, and a spiked tail whips toward my spine.

No time to dodge. My reflexes trigger the temporal stasis weave, freezing the tail three inches from my shoulder blades.

My chest heaves in the dead silence. That was too close. The stasis spell is burned for the rest of the duel; I have to make this opening count.

I layer true sight, wind dampening, and kinetic wards across my skin.

I clap my hands, shattering the stasis and releasing an air burst that flings the dragon back fifty paces.

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 2 && v_reflexes == 4 && v_perception < 4 && v_premonition < 4) {

I loose a lightning bolt straight into his chest. The arc grounds across his scales with zero effect. The silhouette vanishes, and a spiked tail whips toward my spine.

No time to dodge. My reflexes trigger the temporal stasis weave, freezing the tail three inches from my shoulder blades.

My chest heaves in the dead silence. That was too close. The stasis spell is burned for the rest of the duel; I have to make this opening count.

I layer true sight, wind dampening, and kinetic wards across my skin.

I slash Daren's sword into the frozen tail. Stasis shatters with a spray of black blood, the dragon howling in agony as he teleports twenty feet back.

}
