ID: Ch6-Improvise2
TEXT:

"I don't know how you were able to see through my illusion, human, but I'm not going to take it easy on you anymore."

After finishing his phrase, the dragon immediately appears in front of me and swings one of his claws at my chest. It was all I could do to teleport out of harm's way in time, with a short range spell suited for combat.

The dragon and I spend the next few seconds teleporting one after the other, trading rapid-fire displacements across the canopy. This is going nowhere. I detonate an explosion of fire around my body; the shockwave pushes him back, but the flames roll off his scales harmlessly.

Immune to fire, mental compulsion, and illusions. I have catastrophic spells in memory, but casting them without wards will kill Daren, Kate, and Rose. If I drop down and ward them now, I can still unleash full power before the five minutes expire.

choice("Continue fighting with safe spells", Ch6-Elemental3, v_current_scene = Ch6-Elemental3)
choice("Start fighting with bigger spells", Ch6-Big-not-planned, v_current_scene = Ch6-Big-not-planned)


ID: Ch6-Elemental2
TEXT:

"I don't know how you were able to see through my illusion, human, but I'm not going to take it easy on you anymore."

After finishing his phrase, the dragon immediately appears in front of me and swings one of his claws at my chest. It was all I could do to teleport out of harm's way in time, with a short range spell suited for combat.

The dragon and I spend the next few seconds teleporting one after the other and trying to take each other by surprise.

Damn it! If only I could cast my big spells now, I'd make short work of him. I think I can still make it if I go and cast the protection spells on the others right now.

choice("Continue fighting with safe spells", Ch6-Elemental3, v_current_scene = Ch6-Elemental3)
choice("Start fighting with bigger spells", Ch6-Big-not-planned, v_current_scene = Ch6-Big-not-planned)


ID: Ch6-Sword2
TEXT:

"I don't know how you were able to see through my illusion, human, but I'm not going to take it easy on you anymore."

The dragon then breathes fire hotter than ever before towards me. Instinctively, I hold the sword in front of me to defend from his attack. To my surprise, the blade absorbs the dragon's flames, radiating brilliant heat as if set ablaze.

Daren's blade absorbs elemental casts. The enchantments on this steel are incredible.

I slash the sword forward, unleashing the absorbed flames in a concentrated lance of white heat.

The beam strikes his snout dead on. To test the matrix, I channel raw lightning into the steel. Arc-fire crackles across the blade, but when I swing, the lightning grounds across his scales with zero effect, and his claws sweep in for my throat.

I teleport out of range. Fire, lightning, and ice are useless. Air and water lack killing weight. That leaves acid—but will the blade absorb the vitriol, or will the acid dissolve the enchantment?

Only one way to find out.

choice("Use acid on the sword", Ch6-Sword-acid, v_current_scene = Ch6-Sword-acid)
choice("Fight with the sword normally", Ch6-Sword-simple, v_current_scene = Ch6-Sword-simple)


ID: Ch6-Elemental3
TEXT:

#if(v_ch6_defense != 3) {
Warding the others will eat thirty seconds I don't have. I have to make the direct elements work.

I rip slabs of bedrock out of the forest floor with earth magic, hurling them into a spinning kinetic orbit around my body. Any surprise teleport will plunge him into a grinding millstone of granite.

I launch twenty boulders at his chest in rapid succession. Tyrath teleports, but the sheer volume overwhelms his vectors; three slabs hammer his ribs with bone-cracking force. He roars in fury—real damage at last.

I conjure another wave of stone, but Tyrath vents a river of white-hot fire, melting the flying boulders into liquid slag. He dives straight through the molten spray, his breath turning my orbital stones into lava. Liquid rock offers zero kinetic resistance; he ignores the heat completely.

I dismiss the slag and fire a lightning column wide enough to swallow a galley. It grounds across his scales without slowing his dive; I snap-teleport out of his jaws at the last instant.

Acid. I weave an acid sphere around his upper torso. Tyrath unleashes a deafening roar—a concussive sonic blast that blows the acid into harmless vapor. The roar is so loud I have to snap a sound-dampening spell to keep from passing out.

"Insolent wretch!" the dragon screams. "There won't be a single speck of dust left of you when I'm finished!"

Tyrath accelerates his teleports, flashing across the sky faster than I can track. I have godlike mana coursing through my hands, and I can't hold off a single dragon.

}
#if(v_ch6_defense == 3) {
Warding the others will eat thirty seconds I don't have. I have to make the direct elements work.

I rip slabs of bedrock out of the forest floor with earth magic, hurling them into a spinning kinetic orbit around my body. Any surprise teleport will plunge him into a grinding millstone of granite.

I launch twenty boulders at his chest in rapid succession. Tyrath teleports, but the sheer volume overwhelms his vectors; three slabs hammer his ribs with bone-cracking force. He roars in fury—real damage at last.

I conjure another wave of stone, but Tyrath vents a river of white-hot fire, melting the flying boulders into liquid slag. He dives straight through the molten spray, his breath turning my orbital stones into lava. Liquid rock offers zero kinetic resistance; he ignores the heat completely.

I dismiss the slag and fire a lightning column wide enough to swallow a galley. It grounds across his scales without slowing his dive; I snap-teleport out of his jaws at the last instant.

Acid. I weave an acid sphere around his upper torso. Tyrath unleashes a deafening roar—a concussive sonic blast that blows the acid into harmless vapor. My pre-cast sonic ward prevents me from losing consciousness.

"Insolent wretch!" the dragon screams. "There won't be a single speck of dust left of you when I'm finished!"

Tyrath accelerates his teleports, flashing across the sky faster than I can track. I have godlike mana coursing through my hands, and I can't hold off a single dragon.

}
choice("Continue", Ch6-Lose-fight, v_current_scene = Ch6-Lose-fight)


ID: Ch6-Sword-acid
TEXT:

It's all or nothing. If we die here, Daren won't be using this blade anyway.

I channel acid magic into the steel. The metal turns emerald green, hissing with corrosive vapor, but the enchantment absorbs the liquid instead of melting. Daren's blade is a masterpiece.

I teleport onto the dragon's shoulder and drive the blade into his chest. The acid-coated edge cuts through the armor scales like butter, sinking deep into muscle. Tyrath screeches in agony, snap-teleporting away and bathing me in fire.

The blade absorbs the flames, replacing the acid with a radiant fire aura. I fling the fire lance back at him, recast acid across the steel, and teleport onto his flank, carving a deep furrow across his right wing-joint.

For the next minute, Tyrath is forced entirely onto the defensive, wheeling and teleporting to escape my blade. Every strike bites deep. I will bleed him out before the timer expires.

choice("Continue", Ch6-Win-fight, v_current_scene = Ch6-Win-fight, v_ch6_won_dragon = 1)


ID: Ch6-Sword-simple
TEXT:

#if(v_strength < 4) {

I keep the blade clean. The risk of corroding Daren's enchantments is too great.

I teleport beside the dragon and drive the point into his chest.

The steel skitters off the armored scales without biting. Tyrath's right claw lashes out; I parry with the flat, but his tail follows instantly, forcing me to teleport away.

For twenty seconds I dart in and out of melee, striking at every joint, but without superhuman force the blade fails to reach skin.

Now Tyrath seizes the offensive, teleporting faster, forcing me to burn energy on evasions. I can barely track his silhouette. I have godlike power in my veins, and I can't pierce his hide.

}
#if(v_strength == 4) {

I keep the blade clean. The risk of corroding Daren's enchantments is too great.

I teleport beside the dragon and drive the point into his chest with all the force in my arms.

The blade shatters an armor scale and sinks deep into the meat beneath. Tyrath roars through the pain, claw raking my shoulder. I wrench the blade free, parry the strike, and teleport out before his tail connects.

For the next minute, we trade rapid-fire teleports across the sky. Every time he vents fire, Daren's blade absorbs the blast and hurls it back as a white lance. We trade blood for blood, but the clock is ticking down fast.

}
choice("Continue", Ch6-Lose-fight, v_current_scene = Ch6-Lose-fight) if (v_strength < 4)
choice("Continue", Ch6-Win-fight, v_current_scene = Ch6-Win-fight, v_ch6_won_dragon = 2) if (v_strength == 4)


ID: Ch6-Big-not-planned
TEXT:

Trading skirmishes is burning time.

I teleport down to Kate, Daren, and Rose, weaving heavy kinetic and elemental wards around all three to seal them against fallout.

"Barry, what happened?" Daren asks, staring at the mana pouring from my hands. "This power is insane!"

"Explain later. Hold still."

Wards anchored, I shoot back into the sky. Time to go all out.

choice("Continue", Ch6-Big-spells2, v_current_scene = Ch6-Big-spells2)


ID: Ch6-Big-spells2
TEXT:

#if(v_ch6_defense != 3) {
I raise both hands, opening every conduit of power in my mind.

I summon a localized tornado. The vortex rips through the valley, tearing mature pines out by their roots and grinding boulders to gravel.

Tyrath flails against the updraft, while my wind ward keeps me stable. Next, I reach into the bedrock and animate an earth colossus. The earth heaves as a two-hundred-foot stone golem rises from the valley floor, locking two massive granite fists around the dragon's torso.

Tyrath vents a deafening concussive roar that shatters the golem's stone arms to dust. The sonic blast nearly knocks me out, but my wards hold.

Though free, Tyrath is battered and bleeding. He spews white-hot fire, melting the golem's torso into slag.

I open the sky. A deluge of corrosive acid rain pours over the clearing. Tyrath screeches as the acid dissolves his wing membranes, desperately venting fire upward to incinerate the droplets. I teleport above him, slamming him downward with an air cannon. Interrupted, the acid covers his back, burning into raw flesh.

He is broken. The battle is mine.

}
#if(v_ch6_defense == 3) {
I raise both hands, opening every conduit of power in my mind.

I summon a localized tornado. The vortex rips through the valley, tearing mature pines out by their roots and grinding boulders to gravel.

Tyrath flails against the updraft, while my wind ward keeps me stable. Next, I reach into the bedrock and animate an earth colossus. The earth heaves as a two-hundred-foot stone golem rises from the valley floor, locking two massive granite fists around the dragon's torso.

Tyrath vents a deafening concussive roar that shatters the golem's stone arms to dust. My pre-cast sonic ward absorbs the blast.

Though free, Tyrath is battered and bleeding. He spews white-hot fire, melting the golem's torso into slag.

I open the sky. A deluge of corrosive acid rain pours over the clearing. Tyrath screeches as the acid dissolves his wing membranes, desperately venting fire upward to incinerate the droplets. I teleport above him, slamming him downward with an air cannon. Interrupted, the acid covers his back, burning into raw flesh.

He is broken. The battle is mine.

}
choice("Continue", Ch6-Win-fight, v_current_scene = Ch6-Win-fight, v_ch6_won_dragon = 1)


ID: Ch6-Lose-fight
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch6_berserker,1)
set(v_maximized_stats_used,1)
achievement("Berserker mode activated",v_ac_ch6_berserker)
#if(v_ch6_improvise == 2 && v_ch6_offense == 2) {
Rage snaps the restraint in my head. Heat radiates from my skin in visible waves of steam. My perception accelerates tenfold; the dragon's descent slows to a crawl. I don't need the blade.

I sheath Daren's sword. Tyrath's claw sweeps toward my throat; without dodging, I catch the razor talon in my bare left hand.

"No..." Tyrath gasps.

I hold the claw locked and drive my right fist straight into his sternum. The impact shatters his breastplate scales like glass, driving him twenty paces through the air. Blood sprays from his maw. I teleport onto his tail, swinging the massive body and slamming him into the valley floor. The crater throws up a hundred-foot curtain of dust.

One more strike. I dive for the kill—

The power cuts out.

Not a fade. A dead drop. The reservoir in the stat booster is completely empty.

No. Not now. I had him.

The flight spell collapses. I plummet fifty feet toward the rocks.

Three feet from the ground, kinetic stasis catches me. I drop flat on my face into the grass.

"How disappointing," Eiden's voice floats down from the sky. "How very disappointing. I gave you that mana to duel, Barry, not to incinerate it all in five seconds on your device's maximized override."

}
#if(v_ch6_improvise == 1 || v_ch6_offense == 1) {
Rage snaps the restraint in my head. Heat radiates from my skin in visible waves of steam. My perception accelerates tenfold; the dragon's descent slows to a crawl.

