No. Not now. I had him.

The flight spell collapses. I plummet fifty feet toward the rocks.

Three feet from the ground, kinetic stasis catches me. I drop flat on my face into the grass.

"How disappointing," Eiden's voice floats down from the sky. "How very disappointing. I gave you that mana to duel, Barry, not to incinerate it all in five seconds on your device's maximized override."

}
choice(""I don't know what that means."", Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon, v_current_scene = Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon, v_ch6_big_plans = 1)
choice(""I didn't activate anything."", Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon, v_current_scene = Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon, v_ch6_big_plans = 2)
choice(""Why do you keep saving me?"", Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon, v_current_scene = Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon, v_ch6_big_plans = 3)


ID: Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon
TEXT:

#if(v_ch6_big_plans == 1) {
"I don't know what that means."

Eiden sighs.

"Of course you don't," he says. "Look at the dials."

I pull the booster from my pocket.

The numbers on the face are spinning wildly, all attributes red-lined past maximum and crashing back to zero. In my fury, the device channeled the entire five-minute reserve into raw physical enhancement.

"Do you grasp it now, Barry? Mana is finite. Waste it on brute force, and the well runs dry."

"Eiden..." Tyrath rumbles, rising from the crater dust and taking wing. "I have sought you."

Eiden smiles, eyes closed.

"Tyrath! It feels like a century! Or has it been longer? I lose track. Come give your old friend a hug!"

"I intended to draw you out with the ashes of your followers," the dragon snarls. "Today we finish this."

"So melodramatic! You're ruining our reunion."

Tyrath vomits a column of dragonfire. Eiden lifts a single finger; the flame stops in mid-air, reverses direction, and slams back into Tyrath's snout.

"Still your old parlor tricks," Tyrath growls. "I have grown stronger in the centuries since you fled. This will not end as before."

}
#if(v_ch6_big_plans == 2) {
"I didn't activate anything."

Eiden sighs.

"Yes, you did," he says. "You simply weren't paying attention. Look at the dials."

I pull the booster from my pocket.

The numbers on the face are spinning wildly, all attributes red-lined past maximum and crashing back to zero. In my fury, the device channeled the entire five-minute reserve into raw physical enhancement.

"Do you grasp it now, Barry? Mana is finite. Waste it on brute force, and the well runs dry."

"Eiden..." Tyrath rumbles, rising from the crater dust and taking wing. "I have sought you."

Eiden smiles, eyes closed.

"Tyrath! It feels like a century! Or has it been longer? I lose track. Come give your old friend a hug!"

"I intended to draw you out with the ashes of your followers," the dragon snarls. "Today we finish this."

"So melodramatic! You're ruining our reunion."

Tyrath vomits a column of dragonfire. Eiden lifts a single finger; the flame stops in mid-air, reverses direction, and slams back into Tyrath's snout.

"Still your old parlor tricks," Tyrath growls. "I have grown stronger in the centuries since you fled. This will not end as before."

}
#if(v_ch6_big_plans == 3) {
"Why do you keep saving me?"

"Because you have immense potential, Barry. I have grand designs for you."

Grand designs. That sounds ominous.

"Though I question my own judgment when you behave like an amateur."

"I didn't do anything."

Eiden sighs.

"Of course you didn't," he says. "Just look at the dials."

I pull the booster from my pocket.

The numbers on the face are spinning wildly, all attributes red-lined past maximum and crashing back to zero. In my fury, the device channeled the entire five-minute reserve into raw physical enhancement.

"Do you grasp it now, Barry? Mana is finite. Waste it on brute force, and the well runs dry."

"Eiden..." Tyrath rumbles, rising from the crater dust and taking wing. "I have sought you."

Eiden smiles, eyes closed.

"Tyrath! It feels like a century! Or has it been longer? I lose track. Come give your old friend a hug!"

"I intended to draw you out with the ashes of your followers," the dragon snarls. "Today we finish this."

"So melodramatic! You're ruining our reunion."

Tyrath vomits a column of dragonfire. Eiden lifts a single finger; the flame stops in mid-air, reverses direction, and slams back into Tyrath's snout.

"Still your old parlor tricks," Tyrath growls. "I have grown stronger in the centuries since you fled. This will not end as before."

}
choice("Continue", Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon2, v_current_scene = Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon2, v_ch6_won_dragon = 3)


ID: Ch6-Eiden-vs-dragon2
TEXT:

Tyrath lunges, jaws snapping on empty air as Eiden blinks behind his neck and looses a focused lance of white flame. The heat rolls off the scales; Tyrath retaliates with a blistering counter-cone.

Eiden raises an open hand, catching the stream and reversing it into four roaring fire columns that box the dragon in and detonate against his snout.

Why fire? Dragons have near-total immunity to heat. Why waste mana on an element that won't bite?

"Do you mock me, stillwater?" Tyrath roars, shaking off the ash. "Fight with steel or die in the dirt!"

Eiden's smile never slips. He blankets the sky in an ocean of rolling flame, teleporting through the smoke the instant Tyrath closes distance. They flicker across the firmament in a dizzying dance of fire and displacement until the sky itself burns crimson.

Then the earth hums.

A deep, azure luminescence bleeds through the soil beneath our feet. An ancient, suffocating mana pressure saturates the clearing.

"What is the meaning of this?" the dragon asks.

"Has it been so long you've forgotten, old friend?" Eiden says. "Just because they haven't been activated in more than a millennia does not mean these traps are out of function. This one was just a bit out of tune, that's all. So I had to warm it up before it would start working again!"

"You can't mean..."

Eiden's smile widens.

"The lessathi have many flaws, but poor craftsmanship is not one of them. Most of the artifacts they built in the old times are still fully functional after all!"

As the two of them speak, the ground is shaking violently, and the blue light is intensifying.

"Listen to me, stillwater. Your little tricks won't last forever. This won't keep me away for long. And when I get out, you're going to wish you were never born. Do you hear me?! Wipe that smile off your face, you lowborn little--"

All of the magic in the air gets unleashed in a single moment, and the dragon gets teleported away, as the blue light disappears and the earthquake slowly stops.

Eiden turns back to me.

"I hope you won't miss him too much. It'll be a while before we see him again."

choice(""What did you do to him?"", Ch6-Lose-fight2, v_current_scene = Ch6-Lose-fight2, v_ch6_lessathi = 1)
choice(""Who are the lessathi?"", Ch6-Lose-fight2, v_current_scene = Ch6-Lose-fight2, v_ch6_lessathi = 2)


ID: Ch6-Win-fight
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch6_tyrath,1)
achievement("Defeated Tyrath",v_ac_ch6_tyrath)
#if(v_ch6_offense != 2) {
The valley floor thrums.

A deep, azure luminescence bleeds through the soil beneath our feet, radiating an ancient, suffocating mana pressure that makes the hairs on my arms stand up.

"What's... What's happening?..." Tyrath says, trying to hold back the pain.

"Has it been so long you've forgotten, old friend?" I hear Eiden's voice coming from the left.

I turn around and see the stillwater floating in the air next to us, with his usual smile on his face.

"Eiden..." the dragon says.

"Just because these traps haven't been activated in more than a millennia does not mean they are out of function," Eiden continues. "The lessathi of old were anything but shoddy craftsmen. This trap was just a bit out of tune, that's all. Luckily, your continuous use of flames and Barry's volcanoes were just enough to warm it up!" 

As the two of them speak, the ground is shaking violently, and the blue light is intensifying.

"You'll... pay for this... Both of you... I will not rest until I hunt you down. Nowhere on this continent will be safe for you ever again. Do you hear me?! I will hunt you down! Wipe that smile off your face, you lowborn little--"

All of the magic in the air gets unleashed in a single moment, and the dragon gets teleported away, as the blue light disappears and the earthquake slowly stops. The energy from my device is gone. I could sense it disappear the moment the dragon was teleported away.

Eiden turns back to me.

"Well done, Barry! You have far exceeded my expectations!"

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 2 && v_ch6_won_dragon == 1) {
The valley floor thrums.

A deep, azure luminescence bleeds through the soil beneath our feet, radiating an ancient, suffocating mana pressure that makes the hairs on my arms stand up.

"What's... What's happening?..." Tyrath says, trying to hold back the pain.

"Has it been so long you've forgotten, old friend?" I hear Eiden's voice coming from the left.

I turn around and see the stillwater floating in the air next to us, with his usual smile on his face.

"Eiden..." the dragon says.

"Just because these traps haven't been activated in more than a millennia does not mean they are out of function," Eiden continues. "The lessathi of old were anything but shoddy craftsmen. This trap was just a bit out of tune, that's all. Luckily, your continuous use of flames was just enough to warm it up!" 

As the two of them speak, the ground is shaking violently, and the blue light is intensifying.

"You'll... pay for this... Both of you... I will not rest until I hunt you down. Nowhere on this continent will be safe for you ever again. Do you hear me?! I will hunt you down! Wipe that smile off your face, you lowborn little--"

All of the magic in the air gets unleashed in a single moment, and the dragon gets teleported away, as the blue light disappears and the earthquake slowly stops. The energy from my device is gone. I could sense it disappear the moment the dragon was teleported away.

Eiden turns back to me.

"Well done, Barry! I'll be honest with you, I was hoping you'd be using more spectacular spells in this skirmish, but I cannot blame you for wanting to be efficient!"

}
#if(v_ch6_offense == 2 && v_ch6_won_dragon == 2) {
